<body>
    <h1>Feature Sheet - Employee Access</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>The purpose is to affirm the product goals, clarify the feature =
scopes and set the expectation on the conceptual design review for stakehol=
ders.</p>
<h1 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-ProductGoals">Product Goals</h1>
<p>The new Employee Access solution allows CX to be bank-compliant on emplo=
yee access lifecycle management.&nbsp; This means<span>:</span></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9ad834ab-9209-415a-ac2e-16faec2ec46c"><span>Employees sig=
n on to Compass&nbsp;</span>securely via SSO with their bank credentials</l=
i>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9feab071-b0bb-4579-88ba-ec235d52f527">Access creation, mo=
dification, and deactivation requests are handled through standard bank pro=
cesses</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"fe4eb7b8-9405-4665-b781-151eebc3b1f6">Access assignment i=
s proceduralized and respects the principle of least privileges&nbsp;</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"bcfef330-17a3-4c42-8d09-f7208e0b46c9"><span>Employee acce=
ss monitoring is in place and auditable</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d504c6cb-d2ae-480c-b662-20924fa3ff1d"><span>Ongoing emplo=
yee access attestations are supported by bank standard solutions</span></li=
>
</ul>
<h1 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-ProblemSta=
tement">Problem Statement</h1>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;">Bank employees can currently only access Com=
pass-X through direct login with credentials that are unique in Compass, an=
d governed by highly manual attestation processes that may result in misses=
.&nbsp;<span>&nbsp;</span><span>This poses a significant risk of unauthoriz=
ed access due to insufficient controls, which can be easily exploited.&nbsp=
; Since the new Compass launched, the risk has increased due to further dev=
iation from bank standards around access requests and attestations.</span><=
/p>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;"><span>There are currently ~270 NBIN/NBC empl=
oyees affected by this gap.</span></p>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;">This risk has been flagged&nbsp;<span>by bot=
h internal and OSFI audits in 2025 requiring urgent remediation by<strong> =
July 2026.</strong></span></p>
<h1 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-FeatureSco=
pe"><span>Feature Scope</span></h1>
<h3 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-What'sChanging?"><span>What's Changing=
?</span></h3>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;"><span>As a result of introducing this featur=
e:</span></p>
<ul style=3D"text-align: left;">
 <li data-uuid=3D"092edf12-66b2-4a1a-b2d0-42e81363fc2c">All employees as co=
nsumers will no longer access CX or R2 with their current direct external l=
ogins</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"2447632e-8888-4958-914d-746e70448492">Employees and manag=
ers will follow the standard bank process for requesting access to CX, migr=
ating away from Jira Service Desk</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"20eca84a-a9b4-4eac-a5a3-eaeec4d3a78d">Employee user attes=
tations will be introduced for CX</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"0425a884-e5ff-47eb-80c4-59224a5cfc70">Ongoing access matr=
ix maintenance will be introduced for CX</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-InScope">In Scope</h3>
<p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"468" style=3D"width:771px;m=
ax-width: 100%;" src=3D"dca502a87f40a0cd7bd969826a87c7a7c9928e73c07ccc91f81=
540993ecdac0b" height=3D"49"></p>
<p>This feature addresses the full employee access lifecycle:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"b=
fd2e527-1378-4ca3-89ec-9e9fdbd68b05">Employee access request &amp; provisio=
ning flows for both <strong>primary (SSO) AND additional (non-SSO) ID's</st=
rong></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"9=
8baaff7-c4cf-41c3-90a2-6dd124f40f25">Standardized role=E2=80=91based access=
 assignment for primary ID's, and flexible profile setups of additional ID'=
s</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"3=
6232871-305f-4fa8-a11f-33f04e16eee7">Employee access via SSO for primary ID=
's, external login for additional ID's</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"d=
76b11dd-90b4-4de3-8c6d-7fb9dd156f84">Policy-based deactivation, manager/emp=
loyee-triggered deactivation (i.e. job change), and offboarding (departures=
) via IIQ&nbsp;</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"a=
6995080-7f79-44dc-80f0-520ee458535e">Ongoing monitoring &amp; attestations =
via IIQ &amp; annual reporting</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"6=
c1d3552-3820-4fe2-8af0-9d44c45c364b">Visibility and auditability of access =
decisions for both types of ID's</li>
</ul>
<h3 style=3D"text-align: left;" id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-OutofScope=
"><span>Out of Scope</span></h3>
<p style=3D"text-align: left;"><span>What this features does not do:</span>=
</p>
<ul style=3D"text-align: left;">
 <li data-uuid=3D"e3680c9d-0f86-401f-9dec-d696118bbf15">User access adminis=
trators would continue to manage access through CX and R2 separately; in su=
bsequent quarters this will also be unified to eliminate R2 user maintenanc=
e</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9aefdef6-5bf0-4545-a0a8-defb9c0ab961"><span>Manage employ=
ee access to SecuredZone / downstream&nbsp;applications</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"899e5c8a-c655-464d-ace3-23ee353d4e1b"><span>Manage employ=
ees of other business lines - e.g. NBF, NBCSS</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1faad6ba-02f5-4d7b-adbe-b43b640f9e9e"><span>Manage employ=
ees of other internal NBIN applications - i.e. DWH</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d3ac8933-7153-45de-aff5-129a57ca0ad3"><span>"Employee acc=
ounts" in External SSO firms - are these ID's governed by those firms and n=
ot NBIN</span></li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-SolutionOverview">Solution Overview&nb=
sp;</h1>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-EmployeeSetupsinCompass">Employee Setu=
ps in Compass</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 95=
.8383%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 11.8386%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 39.8167%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 48.3292%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Type</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Purpose</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Characteristics</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Primary ID</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"f3dd1153-157b-4f63-9448-4c2d740a85ff">Profile that i=
s used to perform job-related activities in Compass</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"6f0fb761-3748-4086-9e10-cfecbdc113b5">Standardized p=
rofile defined against job function</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"1769ac77-284a-42de-8559-5fa71b5b8822">No modificatio=
ns should be made on feature and data (RR) assignments - linked ID's are op=
en to modifications</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Additional ID</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"4911ad67-9a8c-4d2a-b1d4-ceaad8f25e59">Profile used f=
or secondary or temporary access (typically troubleshooting, project-based,=
 additional profiles that a standard profile cannot accommodate)</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"e6d4b980-7b37-46e5-a408-7a1fb69eb18f">Non-standard p=
rofile dependent on the specific use at the time of provisioning</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"1b3818a7-7a70-4ee5-b237-a2aa3107eea6">Profile config=
uration may change over time, e.g. testing across firms</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-OverviewofIIQCapabilities">Overview of=
 IIQ Capabilities</h2>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 91=
.5451%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 7.54092%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 17.8569%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 17.8569%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 17.8569%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 20.1483%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 18.7618%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">ID Type</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Access requests</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Access&nbsp;provisioning</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Access monitoring</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Access certification</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Access de-provisioning</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Primary ID</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:tick: Initiate from within IIQ</p>
     <p>:tick: Facilitate request approvals</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:tick: Auto-provisioning based on a standard profile definition</p>=
</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:tick: Full profile discrepancies between CX and IIQ will be detect=
ed</p>
     <p>:tick: Job changes (change of function code)</p>
     <p>:warning: Inactivity policy is managed in CX</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:tick: High-privilege profiles are identifiable in IIQ; certificati=
on is facilitated in IIQ</p>
     <p>:tick: Annual certification is facilitated in IIQ&nbsp;</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:tick: IIQ will trigger deactivations and of=
fboarding in CX</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Additional ID's</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:warning: Initiate from myIT (IIQ can only provision into the inter=
nal tenant)</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:cross: Auto-provisioning not supported; manual provisioning via ID=
 Admin</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:tick: Linked back to IIQ employee record (requirement), i.e. no or=
phans</p>
     <p>:warning: Inactivity policy is managed in CX</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>:cross: High-privilege setups cannot be identified by IIQ</p>
     <p>:warning: High-privilege account type is not available in additiona=
l ID's as of 2026</p>
     <p>:question: May require manual annual certification, to be verified =
with Risk Team</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:tick: IIQ will trigger deactivations and of=
fboarding in CX</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-EmployeeAccessMatrixSetup">Employee Ac=
cess Matrix Setup</h2>
<p>To streamline operations (reduce manual intervention on both provisionin=
g and ongoing certifications), profiles have been standardized as much as p=
ossible so that all "pre-packaged" profile definitions are made available t=
o NBIN teams.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 88=
.5662%;">
  <colgroup class=3D"">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 15.2704%;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 36.791%;">
   <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 47.944%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Type</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Setup</th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Restrictions</th>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Primary ID</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"893aa099-931d-4130-aa73-4d441c6e0431">Always in eith=
er NBIN Internal or COR depending on job function</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"c4d6a122-2f27-4bdf-b04f-6799c8956b20">Modules and RR=
 ranges are pre-assigned based on job function</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"4c2c6736-f39a-4652-aaae-67d962fc4ea1">Each team /&nb=
sp;function will have their own profile</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"36e5396c-9379-4844-9f75-67af48b44575">Access via SSO=
 within bank network</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"574e6d8f-2705-42e3-9b1f-f3de88cbcc1e">Profile modifi=
cations in CX will always be reverted to IIQ setup</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Additional ID</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"38da9812-d6d9-4b8b-87bd-4fdcaa076536">Cannot be setu=
p in NBIN Internal (contains high privilege functions and data)</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"eb550974-ba89-4d13-8f4a-c3df4d0686d6">Always setup w=
ithin a firm including COR, and modules / RRs configured in CX based</li>
     </ul></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <ul>
      <li data-uuid=3D"4779a2b2-a64b-439b-b0a8-1eab5a7a68fe">Non-standard p=
rofile dependent on the specific use at the time of provisioning</li>
      <li data-uuid=3D"65c88bc3-d020-413a-b169-e42ba82aba06">Profile config=
uration may change over time, e.g. testing across firms</li>
     </ul></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://cbncnbccs.sharepoint.com/:x:/=
r/sites/Compass-X/Shared%20Documents/Product%20Management/Employee%20Access=
%20Assignment%20Matrix%20(IIQ)/CX%20Access%20Matrix%20Template%20%20-%20DRA=
FT%20v2.xlsx?d=3Dwfe586df08c7d4dee82da888845b2cdd4&amp;csf=3D1&amp;web=3D1&=
amp;e=3DgGYd87" rel=3D"nofollow">CX Access Matrix Template - DRAFT v2.xlsx<=
/a></p>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-EmployeeAccessExperience">Employee Acc=
ess Experience</h2>
<p>Use cases</p>
<ol>
 <li data-uuid=3D"51432c45-0fb9-46c2-a977-104d16a501e5">Primary via IIQ</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"eb37b21a-e11e-40ba-b98a-cf5ccc7d901b">Secondary via stand=
ard request flow=20
  <ol>
   <li data-uuid=3D"25b08f82-e9bc-4a1f-80c2-a4b4126b4ef4">If a firm is not =
specified in the ticket, a user will be created in COR</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3353b8e1-0920-47af-b52f-535116dbea8a">Optional - secondar=
y ID creation on-demand (no request ticket)</li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-AccessOversight&amp;Administration">Ac=
cess Oversight &amp; Administration</h2>
<p>User administration flow</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"980a1de1-7463-43be-90f3-f2e80d9d1c31">Primary via IIQ</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"eb5058e9-3af4-47b9-a0ec-f64a9496494e">Secondary via myIT =
OR Product Support (TBC)=20
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"0cb8ac04-1644-4843-a25c-0217bf9bd15d">Within a firm (in=
cluding COR) a user can be setup to do anything</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"61e50d9b-2ff9-4f16-966f-dd98683a377f">Only authorized u=
sers with Manage Firm &amp; User access can assist in changing secondary ID=
=E2=80=99s</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"c1b09f0b-981e-4f47-89fe-97affd1a0bdd">The change firm f=
eature will only be available in the Manage Firm &amp; User module which is=
 only available NBIN Internal</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"e9154ce2-63d1-4535-b552-8806a1e37ed8">Anyone who has pr=
imary ID that has Manage Firm &amp; User can support managing profile updat=
es</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<p>Ongoing monitoring:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f7eacf34-9e9f-4b17-9ac5-c0053b8cb5c8">User inactivity, or=
phaned accounts, job changes, and offboarding managed in IIQ</li>
</ul>
<p>Ongoing certifications:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1b9a52fc-e404-433c-9404-7ef682722eaf">Quarterly high-priv=
ileged review configured in IIQ</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"f1636814-43e5-45fc-b421-6ea8e614a458">Annual certificatio=
n configured in IIQ - however MAY require annual&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p>Monitoring:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a1fefada-fa0b-4fc4-89a4-7a21a3c91ac7">Governance process =
required for pre-launch access</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b1f88c51-974f-49dd-b90b-54f72823c8a0">Governance process =
required on modifications</li>
</ul>
<p>Reporting:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"01390630-c4a8-48ed-9426-46bf1885ccdb">Generate regular re=
ports to support custodian validation</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"FeatureSheetEmployeeAccess-FeatureLaunches&amp;AccessMatrixMainte=
nance">Feature Launches &amp; Access Matrix Maintenance</h2>
<p>For new feature launches, access matrix + IIQ configuration will need to=
 be refreshed ahead of time to maintain the automation.</p>
<p><br></p>
